  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Participatory Psychosocial Care Approach to of Mental Health in Colombia (PPC-Colombia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deliver significant research funding for internationally competitive and innovative collaborative projects between researchers from Colombia and United Kingdom that will allow the pursuit of shared research interests.
OSA statement says: PPC-Colombia focuses on empowering communities by building their capacity, facilitating access to information on mental health, and co-creating a sustainable model of social intervention rooted in social networks and interaction. The project directly benefits a) Communities and vulnerable groups (the rural, indigenous, Afro-Colombian, women, and adolescents) in the Montes de Maria region; (b) the service providers (Healthcare workers) operating in the area; (c); policy makers (Local health authorities, Ministry of Health and Sciences); (d) researchers at the partnering universities and beyond. Dynamic assessment of impact indicators by all stakeholders and the team will ensure that the project delivers the intended benefits.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world</narrative>
  </description>
